{"name":"Everlasting","hex":"#a1bed9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"everlasting","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Lasting or enduring forever; endless, eternal.\n\nChiefly of a deity or other supernatural being: having always existed and will continue to exist forever; eternal.\n\n Synonym of sempiternal (“having infinite temporal duration, rather than outside time and thus lacking temporal duration altogether”).","Chiefly of a deity or other supernatural being: having always existed and will continue to exist forever; eternal."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Synonym of everlastingly.\n Used as an intensifier: extremely, very.\n\n In an everlasting (adjective sense 1) manner; forever.","Used as an intensifier: extremely, very."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/everlasting"}],"entries":[{"title":"Immortality","blocks":[{"text":"Immortality is the concept of eternal life and permanent resistance to death from natural causes. Some species possess \"biological immortality\" due to an apparent lack of the Hayflick limit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Fountain_of_Eternal_Life_crop.jpg/330px-Fountain_of_Eternal_Life_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immortality"},{"title":"Antennaria","blocks":[{"text":"Antennaria is a genus of dioecious perennial herbs in the family Asteraceae, native to temperate regions of the Northern Hemisphere, with a few species in temperate southern South America; the highest species diversity is in North America. Common names include catsfoot or cat's-foot, pussytoes and everlasting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Antennaria_racemosa_4844f.JPG/330px-Antennaria_racemosa_4844f.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antennaria"},{"title":"Everlasting (Natalie Cole album)","blocks":[{"text":"Everlasting is the eleventh studio album by American singer Natalie Cole, released on June 14, 1987 by Manhattan Records. The album was certified gold by the Recording Industry Association of America (RIAA). Cole earned a nomination for Best Female R&B Vocal Performance at the 1988 Grammy Awards."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1c/Everlasting_Natalie_Cole_album.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Everlasting_(Natalie_Cole_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Telomere_caps.gif/500px-Telomere_caps.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Telomere_caps.gif/500px-Telomere_caps.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Human chromosomes (grey) capped by telomeres (white)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATelomere_caps.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Manhattan%2C_N.Y.C._1997_51.jpg/500px-Manhattan%2C_N.Y.C._1997_51.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Manhattan%2C_N.Y.C._1997_51.jpg/500px-Manhattan%2C_N.Y.C._1997_51.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AManhattan%2C_N.Y.C._1997_51.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Holbein_Danse_Macabre_3.jpg/500px-Holbein_Danse_Macabre_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Holbein_Danse_Macabre_3.jpg/500px-Holbein_Danse_Macabre_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Adam and Eve cond